[{"id":5135380881,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMhexkQ","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"18a86e3880c179d508a1b2597bf5cb2e727b0b92","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\n\n<img width=\"146\" height=\"115\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d73c7aed-818f-498f-9d73-0752ccc12401\" />\n\nFor context, Button already has a similar theme constant which is used to prevent icons from getting oversized when using variable-size textures as icons.\n\nHowever, unlike Button where there's a decent chance of an user-provided icon being used as a button icon, it's much less likely for SpinBox's up/down arrows (you generally use one of your own designs for the entire project). Could you describe some concrete use cases where this theme item is needed? **Buttons Width** already makes it possible to enlarge the buttons for accessibility without needing to edit the icons themselves.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120159#pullrequestreview-5135380881","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120159","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-09-07T21:45:59Z"},{"id":5158149603,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM3Md4w","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"18a86e3880c179d508a1b2597bf5cb2e727b0b92","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","c